  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Randy V\u00e1squez fell apart early, and they never caught up.",
    "what_this_means": "They had the chances. Seven runners in scoring position. But left most of them there. Ty France kept them alive with two home runs and five RBIs, scratching out runs when it mattered least. The offense got ten hits and still trailed from the first inning on. The bullpen did its job after V\u00e1squez exited: Matsui struck out three in 1.2 scoreless, Peralta locked down two more. But nine strikeouts and only two runs produced in RISP situations meant they were always chasing. Texas broke through for six in the opening inning, and the Padres' answer came too late to reset the game. By the time they scored in the fifth and seventh, the deficit had already hardened into permanence.",
    "what_to_watch": "This team keeps finding runs but can't find them in the right order. France gave them two swings when they needed four. The pattern holding steady: enough offense to stay close, never enough early to lead. Ten hits is respectable. Ten strikeouts with only seven runs is a summary of the season so far. The bullpen held what it could. The pitching gave them air. They ran out of at-bats before they ran out of deficit.",
